;; manifest/gftd-retirement.edn — retiring the `gftd` name, per plane.
;;
;; Owner instruction 2026-09-06: "gftd が deprecated なので repo wide に名前を
;; 適切に変えて欲しい", with two choices made when asked: names are decided
;; PER PLANE rather than by one blanket substitution, and the scope reaches
;; the live surfaces (org, domains, keys, jobs).
;;
;; ## Why this file exists before any rename happens
;;
;; The footprint is 86 west projects, 1,816 files in the root tree, 45
;; running launchd jobs, 187 entries under ~/.gftd (signing keys and boot
;; seeds among them), and a large set of *.gftd.ai hosts. A rename that size
;; is not a command, it is a table -- and the table has to be reviewable
;; before anything irreversible runs. What follows is that table, the two
;; things that BLOCK parts of it, and the decisions only the owner can make.
;;
;; ## The standing rules this deliberately overrides
;;
;; CLAUDE.md says twice that this should not be done:
;;
;;   "ドメイン移転で改名しない（登録時点で pin）。名前は discovery alias で
;;    あって identity ではない" -- with IPFS as the example, where io-ipfs and
;;    tech-ipfs-* coexist and BOTH ARE CORRECT.
;;   "一括改名はしない（規則が縛るのは新規登録）" -- for the 77 misplaced
;;    origin-plane repos.
;;
;; The owner was told this and reaffirmed. Recording it here so the next
;; reader finds the conflict resolved rather than unnoticed: the rules stand
;; for ordinary origin drift, and this is an owner decision that a deprecated
;; company identity should not keep naming live infrastructure. CLAUDE.md's
;; two clauses need the exception written into them when the first wave lands.
{:plan/id :gftd-retirement
 :plan/date "2026-09-06"
 :plan/status :in-progress

 :measured
 {:as-of "2026-09-06"
  :west-projects 4337
  :gftd-touching-projects 86
  :name-carries-gftd 32
  :org-gftdcojp-repos 73
  :org-cloud-itonami-repos 13
  :root-tree-files 1816
  :launchd-jobs 45
  :dot-gftd-entries 187
  :method "manifest/west.yml parsed line-wise (the 4-line regex undercounts: it found 71 of 86, because entries carrying `groups:` break its shape); `git grep -lI` over the root tree; `launchctl list`; `ls ~/.gftd`."}

 ;; ── what stops parts of this, measured rather than assumed ──────────────
 :blockers
 [{:id :org-login-rename
   :what "gftdcojp -> <successor>"
   :measured "2026-09-06: this token's X-OAuth-Scopes are admin:public_key, delete_repo, gist, read:org, repo, write:packages. No admin:org. The account IS an org admin (user/memberships/orgs/gftdcojp -> role admin, state active), but the token is not, and an organization's login is changed in the Settings UI rather than through the API in any case."
   :consequence "Cannot be done from here. Owner-in-browser. Everything downstream of it -- 73 repository URLs, every west pin naming them, every deps.edn :git/url, every CI reference -- waits on that one action."
   :status :owner-action-required}
  {:id :dot-gftd-directory
   :what "~/.gftd -> ~/.<successor>"
   :measured "187 entries, including fleet-ci-signer-tip.pem, fleet-ci-signer.pem, aiueos boot seeds (ipns, ml-dsa-65), node DIDs and a murakumo service token. 45 launchd jobs are loaded against it, and GFTD_STATE_DIR / GFTD_ROOT name it."
   :consequence "Moving it is not a rename, it is a cutover: every job reads it while running. Stage it -- create the new path, make the old one a symlink, move jobs one at a time, remove the symlink when the last job is off it. A `mv` breaks the fleet-ci signer and the aiueos boot seeds at once."
   :status :staged-cutover-required}]

 ;; ── the table ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 ;;
 ;; :plane is the one that applies, in ADR-2608040100's order (origin, role,
 ;; family, subject). :why says what the name was carrying that the org path
 ;; already says -- because in every case here, `<org>/<name>` restates the
 ;; org, which CLAUDE.md calls redundant-but-not-wrong. The owner decision is
 ;; that a DEPRECATED origin restated is different from a live one restated.
 ;; ⚠ WAVE 2 CHANGED THIS SECTION. The table below was written from names,
 ;; and names were the wrong thing to read. Measured 2026-09-06, after the
 ;; owner answered the gftd.ai question:
 ;;
 ;;   ALL THIRTEEN cloud-itonami repositories had ALREADY been renamed
 ;;   upstream, to gftd-free names, and the manifest had not followed. Every
 ;;   entry still worked -- through a GitHub redirect, which is exactly what
 ;;   gen-west-manifest.cljs warns about in its own comments: a redirect is
 ;;   not a name, and an old path can later be taken by something else.
 ;;
 ;; So the proposed names below were also wrong: upstream had chosen
 ;; `audio-actor`, not `cloud-itonami-audio-actor` -- the org path already
 ;; says cloud-itonami, and the elision was applied all the way. What wave 2
 ;; actually did was point 10 entries at the names their repositories carry.
 ;; Left as written so the correction is visible rather than tidied away.
 ;;
 ;; Three could not be renamed and the script refused them by name: west.yml
 ;; already had `dougaka`, `dougaka-actor` and `dougaka-vector` as SEPARATE
 ;; entries at the SAME pins -- the same repository registered twice, checked
 ;; out to two paths on disk. A partial migration: three of the four new
 ;; entries were added and all four old ones were left. Removing a duplicate
 ;; is a deletion, not a rename, and both paths have live checkouts, so it is
 ;; its own decision rather than a step in this one.
 :wave-2-result
 {:landed "west.yml commit ec66d5b20f6c6be901ceecc66dfce32a58b81afd, 10 entries"
  :done [["cloud-itonami-gftd-audio-actor" "audio-actor"]
         ["cloud-itonami-gftd-avatar-actor" "avatar-actor"]
         ["cloud-itonami-gftd-illust-actor" "illust-actor"]
         ["cloud-itonami-gftd-motion-actor" "motion-actor"]
         ["cloud-itonami-gftd-rig-actor" "rig-actor"]
         ["cloud-itonami-gftd-sculpt-actor" "sculpt-actor"]
         ["cloud-itonami-gftd-voice-actor" "voice-actor"]
         ["cloud-itonami-ai-gftd-kaisya" "ai-kaisya"]
         ["ai-gftd-dougaka-kagaku" "dougaka-kagaku"]
         ["ai-gftd-dougaka-kodomo" "dougaka-kodomo"]]
  :refused-as-duplicates
  [{:stale "ai-gftd-dougaka" :live "dougaka" :pin "e3aff7e3" :both-checked-out? true}
   {:stale "cloud-itonami-ai-gftd-dougaka-actor" :live "dougaka-actor" :pin "8b491fd5" :both-checked-out? true}
   {:stale "ai-gftd-dougaka-vector" :live "dougaka-vector" :pin "831718a6" :both-checked-out? true}]
  :still-open
  ["ai-kaisya still carries `ai-`, which the taxonomy does not have. The obvious target `kaisya` is a DIFFERENT repository (id 1305773355 vs 1284883752), so this is a naming decision rather than an elision."
   "fleet-db.edn (genpon) still records the old names with :repo-path. `kagami reconcile` absorbs west.yml into it, and its input must be origin/main's west.yml -- not run here."]}

 ;; ── owner answers, 2026-09-06 ───────────────────────────────────────────
 :decisions
 {:org-login "gftdcojp STAYS. No org rename. Repos that belong to itonami (or elsewhere) MOVE; repos that are business records STAY and are archived where they are. This retires the blocker that needed admin:org -- there is nothing to do in Settings."
  :gftd-cli "gftdcojp/gftd -- DELETED 2026-09-06. Owner reaffirmed when told it was irreversible: 紛らわしいので削除.\n\nThe '43 files reference it' figure in the first version of this line was WRONG, and the correction matters more than the count did: the pattern `gftdcojp/gftd\\b` matches `gftd-talent-actor`, `gftd-llm-dataset` and the 1Password vault paths `op://gftdcojp/gftd.resend/...`, because `-` and `.` are word boundaries. Exact references to the REPOSITORY were eight files, five of them generated. The two hand-maintained ones (.gitignore, manifest/repo-bots.edn) are cleaned up in the same commit as this line.\n\nPreserved before deleting, because a reason to remove something is not a reason to lose it: a full mirror bundle at ~/repo-archive/gftdcojp-gftd-20260906.bundle, 94 MB, sha256 2e046ab93d5458d1798d40ffd51a44114630dc1b404ee51f2657cb120c5addad, `git bundle verify` reporting a complete history across main, 251006-shell and three tags. Order was: bundle, verify, unregister from west (01b3b22d), delete on GitHub, clean references. Unregistering before deleting rather than after, so no window exists where the manifest points at a repository that is gone."
  :apps-gftdcojp "業務用 archive. Stays in gftdcojp."
  :kaonavi "250305-jp-gftd-le-case-kaonavi -- 記録用 archive. Stays. A dated case repo is a record of what was filed on that date; renaming it would falsify the record, which is what the plan suspected."
  :dogaka "ai-gftd-dogaka -> unify into dougaka. Measured: it already redirects to cloud-itonami/dogaka, a 3 KB repo distinct from cloud-itonami/dougaka (1284882156). Unifying means retiring dogaka, not renaming it -- the name it would take is occupied by the live one."
  :gftd-ai "All *.gftd.ai resources move to itonami.cloud."}

