 ;; ── apps-gftdcojp: extract or archive, judged per unit ──────────────────
 :apps-gftdcojp-judgement
 {:asked "2026-09-06 — 中身も repo として取り出すか, archive か判断"
  :method "Measured each top level unit for size, recency and whether an equivalent already exists elsewhere in the workspace. Original work that exists nowhere else is worth extracting; everything else is a record."
  :extract
  [{:unit "00-contracts/lexicons" :size "34 MB, 8,722 files"
    :why "8,377 of them are ai.gftd.* — the organisation's OWN AT Protocol NSIDs. kotoba-lang/org-bluesky-atproto carries one json file, so this exists nowhere else. It is the single largest piece of original work in the repository, and 34 of the 35 MB of 00-contracts."
    :warning "⚠ The namespace is under the retiring domain. If gftd.ai moving to itonami.cloud is followed through, ai.gftd.* becomes cloud.itonami.* — and AT Protocol NSIDs are WIRE identifiers, not names: renaming them breaks every record already written under them. Extract the repository now; treat the namespace as a separate protocol decision with its own migration."}
   {:unit "arxiv" :size "116 KB"
    :why "A complete LaTeX paper — main.tex, main-ja.tex, references.bib, three figure sources, a Makefile — titled 'ai-gftd-organism: Realizing an Information Life Form'. Distinct from com-junkawasaki/moex, which is a different paper (MoEx / WebGPU) and is the established shape for a paper repository here."}]
  :archive
  [{:unit "50-infra" :size "126 MB"
    :why "95 MB of it is vultr/geth-private, whose bulk is four VENDORED submodules (forge-std, solady, coinbase/smart-wallet, openzeppelin-contracts-v4) rather than original work. The live infrastructure now lives per-repo plus the fleet."}
   {:unit "_working" :size "106 MB"
    :why "106 of the 106 MB is malak — the evidence directory. That is a retention question, not an extraction candidate. keiei, murakumo and transform-drafts are drafts under 1 MB between them."}
   {:unit "90-docs" :size "9.7 MB" :why "2604xx design documents. A record by definition."}
